@startuml google-iap-sequence
title Google Play IAP - recommended end-to-end flow (consumables)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor       Player
participant "Moskha Unity Game\n(Unity IAP)"            as Unity
participant "Google Play\n(on device)"            as Play
participant "Backend" as API
database    "Moksha Database"    as DB
participant "Google Play\nDeveloper API"          as GApi
queue       "Pub/Sub\n(RTDN)"                     as PubSub

== 1. Buy on device ==
Player -> Unity : Tap "Buy 1000 gems"
Unity -> Play : InitiatePurchase(productId,\n obfuscatedAccountId = hash(userId))
Play -> Player : Payment sheet (card / UPI / wallet)
Player -> Play : Confirm payment

alt Payment completes later (UPI / cash) -> Google state PENDING (2)
    Play --> Unity : Purchase PENDING
    Unity -> Player : "Payment processing..." (grant nothing)
    note over Play, Unity : When payment completes, Play delivers the\npurchase again as PURCHASED (continue below).\nIf it never completes it is cancelled - no charge.
end

Play --> Unity : Purchase PURCHASED\n(receipt: purchaseToken, orderId, productId)
Unity -> Unity : ProcessPurchase -> return Pending\n(keep transaction open, do NOT grant locally)

== 2. Server validation (validate-google-purchase) ==
Unity -> API : POST /api/purchase/validate-google-purchase\nJWT + {productId, purchaseToken, packageName}
API -> API : userId from JWT\ncheck productId in server catalog\npackageName == configured package

API -> DB : Find by purchaseToken
alt Token already processed for SAME user
    DB --> API : existing (Purchased)
    API --> Unity : 200 OK {status: AlreadyGranted, seenBefore: true}
    note right of Unity : Idempotent retry (crash / lost response).\nClient just finishes the purchase (step 3).
else Token belongs to ANOTHER user
    API --> Unity : 409 Conflict
else New token
    API -> GApi : purchases.products.get(package, productId, token)
    alt Google 400/404/410 (fake or expired token)
        GApi --> API : error
        API -> DB : log attempt (does NOT block token)
        API --> Unity : 422 Invalid purchase
    else Google 5xx / timeout
        GApi --> API : error
        API --> Unity : 503 Retry later (nothing stored)
    else purchaseState = 2 (PENDING)
        GApi --> API : pending
        API -> DB : upsert state = Pending
        API --> Unity : 202 Pending (keep transaction open)
    else purchaseState = 1 (CANCELLED)
        GApi --> API : cancelled
        API -> DB : save state = Cancelled
        API --> Unity : 422 Cancelled
    else purchaseState = 0 (PURCHASED)
        GApi --> API : orderId, purchaseTime, consumptionState,\nacknowledgementState, obfuscatedExternalAccountId,\npurchaseType (test?), quantity
        API -> API : obfuscatedExternalAccountId == hash(userId)?
        group Single DB transaction
            API -> DB : INSERT purchase_transaction\n(state = Purchased, UNIQUE purchase_token)
            API -> DB : Grant rewards to wallet / inventory
        end
        API -> GApi : purchases.products.consume(package, productId, token)
        GApi --> API : 204 OK
        API -> DB : MarkAsConsumed() (IsConsumed = true, ConsumedAt)
        API --> Unity : 200 OK {status: Granted, rewards, newBalance}
    end
end

== 3. Finish on device ==
Unity -> Play : ConfirmPendingPurchase(product)
note right of Play : Clears Unity's local queue.\nConsume already done server-side.
Unity -> Player : Show 1000 gems

== 4. Safety net (background job, every few hours) ==
API -> DB : Find Purchased AND IsConsumed = false (older than 1h)
API -> GApi : purchases.products.consume (retry)
API -> DB : MarkAsConsumed()
note over API : Alert if any purchase is close to the\n3-day limit (Google auto-refunds after that).

== 5. Refund / chargeback (any time later) ==
GApi -> PubSub : voidedPurchaseNotification(purchaseToken)
PubSub -> API : POST /api/google/rtdn (push)
API -> GApi : (or poll) voidedpurchases.list
API -> DB : state = Refunded
API -> DB : Deduct granted gems (balance may go negative),\nflag account if repeated
@enduml
